lk about the series as a whole  instead of just selector infected Vic  Ross the first season because the  premise more or less remains similar for  each season young girls playing a card  game where winning allows them to have a  wish granted however a dark twist awaits  at the end of each road to glory not  only do the characters have their wishes  overturned and reversed if they lose  often enough and even darker fate lies  at the end of their journey if it  reminds you of something congratulations  I've just introduced you to Madoka with  trading cards the turn and the overall  feel of the anime varies between seasons  but they all follow one generally  streamlined narrative I also like how  each series follows a new protagonist  who still gets to interact with familiar  faces from the previous seasons giving  the whole thing a sense of continuity  licensing and possibly trust issues  between companies means that the actual  card game would likely never see an  English release which off the bat hurts  the popularity of the series nonetheless  I think that the series is worth a look  and I found myself really enjoying how  the story developed through its four  connected seasons  moving on past the darkness of girls  doing things for the sake of wishes how  about a literature inspired romantic  comedy boarding school Juliet is at  number eight we've had countless  literary inspired titles over the course  of anime history but this is one title  that caught my eye in particular towards  the end of 2018 set in a more modern  world boarding school Juliet takes a  more relatable approach in telling the  story of Romeo and Juliet's forbidden  love this time the setting takes place  in Dalia Academy the melting pot for two  countries embroiled in a bitter feud the  black doggies and the white cats have  themselves a long-standing feud led by  their leaders Romeo inuzuka and Juliet  Persia the thing is the two leaders are  actually really really in love with each  other with the feud between the houses  that's an all-time high the couple just  has to come to terms with the fact that  they might be forced to keep their  relationship a secret forever with  prying eyes from friends and rivals  alike how much longer can they keep this  act up I got drawn into the series due  to the cute character designs and the  premise that somehow reminded me of  Nyssa coy at first and I'd say that the  series needs a lot more love than it  actually got the scenarios were fun and  enjoyable and I liked the development of  the side characters in particular the  author has done a really great job of  creating some lovable characters and a  lot of funny incidents to put them in  making this a really fun watch if you're  looking to unwind with some rom-coms  airing in a season with waifu wars  generator Nisekoi supernatural fantasy  noragami ever beloved space dandy and me  material pupa there's a cute little show  about teenage drama with a dash of  Japanese spiritualism yes I'm not  surprised that NRI kon Kon was one of  the underrated shows in that particular  season given the strength of the season  I believe that this title is actually at  its proper place in that seasons  popularity charts however that doesn't  change the fact that I think this is one  heartwarming series that more people  should watch and appreciate the story  premise is simple enough middle school  girl finds herself hopelessly in love  cries about her inability to confess it  to shrine and the shrines goddess grants  her the power to transform well turns  out being in love isn't as easy as being  able to pretend to be someone else in  order to make your confession especially  if you've gotten yourself involved in  the affairs of gods and spirits in the  process  Inari Khan Khan offers what a standard  anime of this genre typically gives cute  heartwarming moments some magic  sprinkled in and a fun and adorable cast  of characters despite its shorter than  usual 10 episode run the show manages to  hit its mark personally I prefer the  more action Ishaan Rah's but even I was  charmed by this show and I think that  you should give it a shot too  so tell us okay go  you know with the wake of the attack on  Titan phenomenon in 2013 those who  prepare anime can't help but green light  those dystopian humanity vs. monster  shows in order to ride the wave so we  got stuff like syrup of the end or  carbon Airy of the iron fortress or  black bullet among these I think that  the one that went under the radar the  most was gordita now I honestly think  this show needed more love sure is Noah  near the masterpiece that it was trying  to ride the momentum front but so are  the other three shows that I mentioned I  think that as a game adaptation gordita  is fine it goes with a tried and true  story of humanity fighting for survival  against monsters with their special  equipment meant to combat those threats  the CG art might be the breaking point  for a lot of fans during its time but I  never felt that the art completely  hampered my enjoyment of seeing amazing  intense fights in the series it's an  acquired taste but after having seen  stuff like our Jian and Knights of  Cydonia I think that I stopped letting  our affect my enjoyment unless of course  it's something as horrible as re fear at  those monsters now that was something  else  I can see that God Eater started off  pretty dull but after a few episodes I  found myself enthralled with the  characters fight for survival if you're  up for some popcorn anime before the  next season of attack on Titan you  should definitely go for this show  remember the good old days when we got a  lot of visual novel adaptations the  genre slowed down drastically this past  decade but every once in a while we  still get some surprisingly great ones  one such title is 2016 so no kanata no  for rhythm shortened as O'Connor set in  a futuristic world where man has finally  conquered the skies people go around  flying in grav shoes footwear that allow  people to defy gravity and fly so people  came up with flying circus a sport that  fully utilizes such wonders of  technology in simple terms Arcana is a  Sports anime centered on bright and  optimistic  Oscar Korra Sheena and her friends at  the FC club at school it's more or less  your standard sports title so you kind  of know what to expect in addition to  the character designs that drew me into  the series our first what I found in our  kana is a surprisingly deep story for my  expectations that let me empathize with  the characters and the challenges they  face our Ghana  really does a good job at showing the  journey from newbie into someone  becoming good at the sport as well as  some moments that showcase the  satisfaction of winning and the heart  breaks into feet whatever your saves on  this I believe that our Ghana is one of  the underrated gems from the past few  years  [Music]  Kosciuszko  hatsune chica  our fourth spot is what I think is an  even better sports anime this time it's  a manga adaptation that debut just  recently in late 2018 run with the wind  tells the story of God guru who starts  this tale on quite the wrong side of the  law narrowly evading consequence for  shoplifting he runs into [ __ ] who  invites him to live with him in a  run-down apartment  given that Garg arrow isn't in the best  place financially he accepts the  invitation and finds himself at the  headquarters of the conse University  track club it's there that [ __ ] reveals  his goal he wants to win it all at the  biggest university marathon relay race  in Japan problem is the rest of the dorm  mates and novice runners and they're not  even interested  somehow the premise might remind you of  our hero no sora another sports anime  that i think needs a bit more love -  when i first took a look at it a lot of  people have praised run with the wind  but i just think that the genre is not  doing so hot right now in terms of  popularity  except for maybe high q-- it doesn't  help that it came out alongside headline  grabber goblin slayer bunny girl sent by  zombie land saga and the new seasons of  sao as well as index i personally give  the recommendation to watch run with the  wind one of the most underrated shows of  that particular season in our third  place is a movie when Marnie was there  takes the third spot  being the only anime film on this  edition of this list anime films have  been gaining ground the past couple of  years in no large part thanks to the  masterpieces of filmmakers let Shinkai  as well as the sudden urge in releasing  said films outside of japan however lost  in the shuffle of the flood of emotional  and artistic anime films is the dramatic  tale based on the classic children's  novel when Marnie was there basically  tells the story of our protagonist Anna  whose health conditions forced her into  living in Sapporo there she finds an  abandoned mansion and starts a series of  encounters with the girl that she sees  in her dreams as the story goes on the  mystery surrounding the girl from Anna's  dreams and her relation to the rest of  Anna's family begins to unravel in a  rollercoaster of emotions given the  pedigree oh she blew in the anime  movie markets I'm not surprised that  when Marnie was there ended up being  underappreciated it didn't live up to  films like spirited away or toward or oh  when it comes to capturing the hearts of  many but I still think that you should  really give this film a shot the classic  Ghibli film traits of amazing artwork  and fantastic storytelling are there and  I think that this is one of the films  that really made me emotional in the way  it delivered its drama it also has a lot  of themes that can hit close to home  especially for those having troubles  with family acceptance and abandonment  it's a tearjerker film that really  deserves a bit more popularity than what  it currently has Mononoke is the  adaptation of a Japanese horror  anthology centered on the medicine  cellar and his journey across Japan  defeating evil spirits along the way  Mononoke for me gives itself a unique  edge over the other evil spirits Lange  shows by not just being about  superpowers and exciting action for the  medicine cellar to defeat an evil spirit  he has to get to know it first this  includes getting information such as its  form origin and motive this opens up a  lot of possibilities as some of the  spirits tend to be quite the Troublesome  ones to analyze I think that there are  people who would love this style in  comparison to the more action-packed  style of shows in this genre like bleach  and Demon Slayer for just a slight  change of pace the show also sets itself  apart from its contemporaries with its  eye-catching art style it might take a  while to get used to scenes and  character designs reminiscent of ancient  Japanese art but I think that the art  style is exactly part of the show's  charm Mononoke is a surprisingly  intricate and deep look at the  supernatural genre and I definitely  consider it not only underappreciated  but one of the best horror anime out  there period  now where do I start with Astra lost in  space I admit that it's a show that I  didn't have the strong impression of at  first but the way the story develop just  made me a believer I'm sure that the  same opinion is the general opinion of  the anime community and it's the biggest  reason why for me the three episode rule  isn't completely a good way of looking  at things three episodes just isn't  enough for one to appreciate the amazing  ride Astra lost in space ended up being  what started out being an okay premise  of friends being lost in space ended  being one of the best space dramas I've  seen for such a long time Astra lost in  space really excels as showing the  struggles in the fight to overcome outer  space in order to battle their way back  home ironic that I use the word battle  because the series doesn't really have a  lot of that instead the dialogue and the  presentation do the heavy lifting and  helping you empathize with the  characters who are really well developed  by the way you don't see this much care  put in making characters these days and  it truly makes Astra lost in space as  standout in the saturation of characters  in modern anime the show can admittedly  be a drag at first which I think caused  it to be underappreciated still I really  recommend this because it turned out to  be one of the best surprises in the  season I go with the consensus of this  show being one that eventually grew out  to be among the top shows in the whole  of 2019 how's that for the third volume  of our underrated anime if you've seen  these shows make sure to let your  friends in the comments section know do  you think that they deserve more  popularity than what they have why or  why not  don't forget to leave a like if you  enjoyed the video if we get 15,000 likes  again I will consider making another  volume don't forget to subscribe if you  want to see more content like this the  bell buttons also there so you can be  the first in line the next time I upload  a new video till we meet again  [Music]
 

